[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Read by what each report
says, and by the tenant and form it came through, it holds three problems. The queued parser fix
closes only the first. Each problem now has its own ticket.

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix will not stop the other two. Keep #4471 open for the parser only, and track the
form hint and the one-day move on their own tickets.
</Callout>

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** A tenant whose locale writes the
day first gets day and month swapped: "Booked for 2 March. The invite says 3 February." This is
the bug #4471 describes, and the queued fix is for it.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form tells people to type month first.** Its date field shows the hint
`MM/DD/YYYY`, so people type the month first, and the form then reads the date the tenant's way,
day first. The dates come out swapped too, so they look like the parser bug, but the parser fix
does not touch them. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants land here.

**`one-day`: the date moves by one day.** These reports describe no swap at all: "Invite says
Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto
got Monday." The desk already noted them (`desk-notes.json`), but the cause table files them
under `parser` because of their tenant. A date that shifts by a day points at time zones, not at
date order.

## Why they were merged

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. All three
  problems produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so they all
  landed in #4471.
- Intake's `intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser. It often disagrees with the
  tenant, in both directions, so it cannot be used to split them.
- The export pages overlap: some reports appear twice. Count by id.

## For the desk

- When a report's dates are swapped, check the tenant's form before merging: a booking-v3 form
  report goes to the hint ticket.
- When a date moved by one day, it is not a swap. File it on the one-day ticket.
- Reopen decision 0001 with a new record: subject alone hides different problems.

